WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.278
Meet the Copilot Credit Estimator.

2
00:00:03.278 --> 00:00:05.562
In about a minute, it turns a

3
00:00:05.562 --> 00:00:09.500
plain-English idea into a monthly credit
estimate.

4
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.971
First, pick what you're estimating.

5
00:00:12.971 --> 00:00:16.641
Copilot Studio agents is the default.

6
00:00:16.641 --> 00:00:21.600
If you're planning Cowork, flip the switch
up top.

7
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.849
Next, choose how to estimate.

8
00:00:23.849 --> 00:00:28.036
There are four ways in, but if you're
early or unsure,

9
00:00:28.036 --> 00:00:32.300
start with Quick, and just describe the
agent in words.

10
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:35.425
In the box, say what the agent does,

11
00:00:35.425 --> 00:00:39.071
who uses it, how often, and where it runs.

12
00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:40.547
No jargon needed.

13
00:00:40.547 --> 00:00:44.800
Or click an example chip to start from a
pattern.

14
00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:47.994
When you're ready, select Build my
estimate.

15
00:00:47.994 --> 00:00:50.534
The tool reads your description and

16
00:00:50.534 --> 00:00:53.800
pre-fills a short, guided assessment for
you.

17
00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:58.940
Now just confirm a few quick questions, or
skip straight to results.

18
00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:02.567
On the right, your live estimate updates
in real

19
00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:06.800
time: the build size, the monthly credits,
and the cost.

20
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:07.909
That's it.

21
00:01:07.909 --> 00:01:16.007
From here, refine in Detailed, compare
licensing, or estimate the return.

22
00:01:16.007 --> 00:01:20.000
Clear numbers, in under two minutes.

